Build a full-stack eBay Repricer Web App

## Objective

Build a production-ready web application that automatically reprices a user’s eBay listings against approved competitor listings. The app must support user accounts, connect each user’s eBay store via OAuth, import and refresh active listings, compute min/max price bounds (based on fees, shipping, ROI), and reprice within those bounds according to user strategies. Users must review/approve suggested competitor listings before any price competition occurs.

## Tech & Architecture (use defaults unless stated)

* **Backend:** TypeScript + Node.js (NestJS or Express + Zod for validation).
* **Frontend:** React + TypeScript (Next.js App Router) with Tailwind CSS.
* **DB:** PostgreSQL + Prisma ORM (include migrations).
* **Background jobs:** BullMQ (Redis) for scheduled/queued tasks.
* **Auth:** Email/password + session (NextAuth or custom JWT w/ httpOnly cookies).
* **Secrets/config:** Dotenv; never hard-code secrets. Provide `.env.example`.
* **eBay APIs:** Use OAuth2 and the **Sell** & **Trading**/**Finding**/**Buy Browse** APIs via a clean “eBayAdapter” interface.

  * Implement the adapter with pluggable search methods so we can switch between **Finding API** or **Buy Browse API** depending on access.
  * Implement Sell Inventory/Feed calls as placeholders where needed; include mocks and real calls behind feature flags.
* **API boundaries:** REST (JSON) under `/api/v1/*`. Use OpenAPI (Swagger) auto-docs.
* **Security:** Input validation with Zod; RBAC (role: USER, ADMIN); rate-limit public endpoints; CSRF protection on forms; secure cookie flags.
* **Testing:** Unit (Jest), API (supertest), e2e (Playwright). Include a seed script.

## Core User Stories & Acceptance Criteria

### 1) User Accounts & Login

* Users can sign up (email + password), sign in, reset password via email token.
* Sessions stored securely. Admin role toggle via DB.
* Acceptance: Auth routes, tests, and guarded API routes exist.

### 2) Connect eBay Store (OAuth2)

* User clicks “Connect eBay,” completes OAuth, tokens (access + refresh) saved encrypted per user.
* Store metadata saved (username, store id).
* Token refresh handled automatically (scheduled job + on-demand).
* Acceptance: Successful token exchange and refresh; errors surfaced to UI; tokens never exposed on client.

### 3) Import Active Listings (initial + daily + on-demand)

* On first connect: import all active listings (listingId, title, SKU, item price, shipping cost, total price = item + shipping, quantity, condition, category, item specifics).
* Nightly job re-syncs active listings; on-demand “Sync Now” button.
* Acceptance: Listings appear in “Products” grid with latest data; lastSyncAt updated; errors visible in an “Activity Log”.

### 4) Product Min/Max Price Bounds

* Each product row stores:

  * **itemCost**, **shippingLabelCost**, **ebayFinalValueFeePct** (default per user, overridable per product), **roiMinPct**, **roiMinDollar** (user can set one or both; if both set, use the **higher** requirement), **minPrice**, **maxPrice** (derived or user-locked).
* Provide **auto-calc** buttons to compute `minPrice` and `maxPrice` from:

  * `priceBase = itemCost + shippingLabelCost + (ebayFinalValueFeePct * targetPrice)`
  * ROI rules:

    * Percent: `targetPrice >= priceBase * (1 + roiMinPct)`
    * Dollar: `targetPrice >= priceBase + roiMinDollar`
  * Choose the **greater** target from percent/dollar rule as the min bound.
  * `maxPrice` default: `minPrice * 1.5` (editable).
* All “Price” values mean **item price + shipping** (total ask).
* Acceptance: UI shows current min/max; recalculates on edit; server validates bounds.

### 5) Competitor Discovery & Approval

* For each product, user can define competitor search **keywords** (default seed from product title; user-editable).
* System fetches competitor listings (search by keywords + category; filter out same seller).
* User reviews the returned candidates in a **“Competitor Matches”** tab:

  * Show title, seller, total price (item + shipping), condition, feedback score, shipping speed.
  * User **Approve** ✅ or **Deny** ❌ each. Only approved items are used for pricing decisions.
* Store normalized competitor snapshots so we can price even if listing disappears temporarily.
* Acceptance: Approved competitors persist; deny list prevents re-suggestion for N days.

### 6) Repricing Strategy & Execution

* Strategy options per product:

  * **Match lowest approved competitor** total price.
  * **Beat by amount** (e.g., `$1 lower`) or **beat by percent** (e.g., `1% lower`).
  * **Stay above** (e.g., `$1 higher`) if ROI margin is abundant.
  * Rounding rules: to nearest `$0.01`, `$0.05`, `$0.10`, or custom tick.
  * Floor/ceiling enforcement: never go below `minPrice`, never above `maxPrice`.
* Repricing formula:

  * `competitorTarget = f(lowestApprovedCompetitorTotalPrice)`
  * `candidateTotal = round(floor/ceil(competitorTarget, strategy))`
  * `finalTotal = clamp(candidateTotal, minPrice, maxPrice)`
  * Then split `finalTotal` into **itemPrice** and **shipping** according to the product’s shipping policy (if shipping is fixed/known, adjust itemPrice = finalTotal - shipping).
* Reprice triggers:

  * Nightly job, hourly job, and **on-demand** per product or bulk selection.
* eBay update:

  * Update listing item price via appropriate eBay Sell/Trading API.
  * Log the change with before/after totals, chosen competitor reference, and strategy reason.
* Acceptance: Dry-run mode shows the proposed new prices; live mode updates eBay and logs.

### 7) Activity Log & Audit

* Every sync, competitor import, approval/deny, and price update creates a log entry with timestamp, user, and payload snapshot.
* UI page “Activity Log” with filters (type/date/product) + CSV export.

### 8) Dashboards & Tables

* **Dashboard:** KPIs (connected stores, active listings, % with min/max set, # awaiting competitor approval, last 24h price changes).
* **Products table:** search, filter, sort; inline editing for cost/fees/ROI; bulk actions (recalc min/max, reprice dry-run/live).
* **Competitors tab per product:** candidate list, approved list, denied list.
* **Settings:** user default fees, default ROI rules, rounding rule, time zone, scheduling preferences.

